{"id":"mahabharata-1-216","work":"mahabharata","part":1,"partName":"आदिपर्व","partNameEn":"Adi Parva","unit":216,"title":"षोडशाधिकद्विशततमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 216 · Gandiva and the discus","summary":{"en":"Agni calls on Varuna, who gives Arjuna the bow Gandiva with two inexhaustible quivers and a chariot with white horses and the monkey banner, and gives Krishna the discus and a mace. The two take their places on either side of the forest, and Agni begins to burn it.","kn":"ಅಗ್ನಿಯ ಕರೆಗೆ ವರುಣನು ಬಂದು ಅರ್ಜುನನಿಗೆ ಗಾಂಡೀವ ಧನುಸ್ಸು, ಎರಡು ಅಕ್ಷಯ ಬತ್ತಳಿಕೆಗಳು, ಬಿಳಿ ಕುದುರೆಗಳ ಕಪಿಧ್ವಜ ರಥವನ್ನೂ, ಶ್ರೀಕೃಷ್ಣನಿಗೆ ಚಕ್ರ ಗದೆಗಳನ್ನೂ ನೀಡುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಇಬ್ಬರೂ ಕಾಡಿನ ಎರಡು ಬದಿಗಳಲ್ಲಿ ನಿಲ್ಲುತ್ತಾರೆ, ಅಗ್ನಿ ಸುಡಲಾರಂಭಿಸುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"अग्नि के आह्वान पर वरुण अर्जुन को गाण्डीव धनुष, दो अक्षय तूणीर और श्वेत घोड़ों तथा कपिध्वज वाला रथ, और श्रीकृष्ण को चक्र और गदा देते हैं। दोनों वन के दोनों ओर खड़े होते हैं, और अग्नि उसे जलाना आरम्भ करते हैं।","te":"అగ్ని పిలుపుకు వరుణుడు వచ్చి అర్జునునికి గాండీవ ధనుస్సు, రెండు అక్షయ తూణీరాలు, తెల్ల గుర్రాల కపిధ్వజ రథాన్ని, శ్రీకృష్ణునికి చక్రం, గదను ఇస్తాడు. ఇద్దరూ అడవికి ఇరువైపులా నిలబడతారు, అగ్ని దహించడం ప్రారంభిస్తాడు.","ta":"அக்னியின் அழைப்பால் வருணன் வந்து அர்ஜுனனுக்குக் காண்டீவ வில், இரண்டு அள்ளக் குறையாத அம்பறாத்தூணிகள், வெண்குதிரைகள் பூட்டிய குரங்குக் கொடித் தேர் ஆகியவற்றையும், ஸ்ரீகிருஷ்ணருக்குச் சக்கரம், கதை ஆகியவற்றையும் அளிக்கிறான். இருவரும் காட்டின் இரு பக்கங்களிலும் நிற்க, அக்னி எரிக்கத் தொடங்குகிறான்.","ml":"അഗ്നി വരുണനെ വിളിക്കുന്നു; വരുണൻ അർജുനന് രണ്ട് അക്ഷയ ആവനാഴികളുള്ള ഗാണ്ഡീവം എന്ന വില്ലും, വെള്ളക്കുതിരകളും കുരങ്ങിന്റെ കൊടിയുമുള്ള രഥവും നൽകുന്നു; കൃഷ്ണന് ചക്രവും ഗദയും നൽകുന്നു. ഇരുവരും വനത്തിന്റെ ഇരുവശങ്ങളിലും നിലയുറപ്പിക്കുന്നു, അഗ്നി അതിനെ ദഹിപ്പിക്കാൻ തുടങ്ങുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 1.216; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Thu Aug 22 2026","sections":[{"title":"खाण्डवदाहपर्व","titleEn":"Khandavadaha Parva (Burning of the Khandava forest)","verses":[{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"एवमुक्तस्तु भगवान्धूमकेतुर्हुताशनः ।\nचिन्तयामास वरुणं लोकपालं दिदृक्षया ।\nआदित्यमुदके देवं निवसन्तं जलेश्वरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thus addressed, the holy Agni, he of the smoke banner, the eater of oblations, wished to see Varuna, guardian of the world, the Aditya god who dwells in the waters as lord of the waters, and thought of him."}},{"n":2,"text":"स च तच्चिन्तितं ज्ञात्वा दर्शयामास पावकम् ।\nतमब्रवीद्धूमकेतुः प्रतिपूज्य जलेश्वरम् ।\nचतुर्थं लोकपालानां रक्षितारं महेश्वरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Knowing his thought, Varuna showed himself to Agni. Agni, with due honor to the lord of the waters, the fourth of the world-guardians and the great protector, spoke to him."}},{"n":3,"text":"सोमेन राज्ञा यद्दत्तं धनुश्चैवेषुधी च ते ।\nतत्प्रयच्छोभयं शीघ्रं रथं च कपिलक्षणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Give me quickly both the bow and the two quivers that King Soma gave you, and the chariot bearing the monkey emblem."}},{"n":4,"text":"कार्यं हि सुमहत्पार्थो गाण्डीवेन करिष्यति ।\nचक्रेण वासुदेवश्च तन्मदर्थे प्रदीयताम् ।\nददानीत्येव वरुणः पावकं प्रत्यभाषत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Partha will do a very great work with Gandiva, and Vasudeva with the discus; let them be given to me for that purpose. I will give them, Varuna replied to Agni."}},{"n":5,"text":"ततोऽद्भुतं महावीर्यं यशःकीर्तिविवर्धनम् ।\nसर्वशस्त्रैरनाधृष्यं सर्वशस्त्रप्रमाथि च ।\nसर्वायुधमहामात्रं परसेनाप्रधर्षणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then he gave that wondrous jewel of a bow, of great power, that increases fame and renown, unassailable by all weapons and crushing all weapons, the chief of all arms, overwhelming enemy armies,"}},{"n":6,"text":"एकं शतसहस्रेण संमितं राष्ट्रवर्धनम् ।\nचित्रमुच्चावचैर्वर्णैः शोभितं श्लक्ष्णमव्रणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"equal by itself to a hundred thousand bows, a bow that makes kingdoms prosper, bright with varied colors, smooth and flawless,"}},{"n":7,"text":"देवदानवगन्धर्वैः पूजितं शाश्वतीः समाः ।\nप्रादाद्वै धनुरत्नं तदक्षय्यौ च महेषुधी ॥","meaning":{"en":"honored for endless years by gods, danavas and gandharvas; and he gave the two great inexhaustible quivers."}},{"n":8,"text":"रथं च दिव्याश्वयुजं कपिप्रवरकेतनम् ।\nउपेतं राजतैरश्वैर्गान्धर्वैर्हेममालिभिः ।\nपाण्डुराभ्रप्रतीकाशैर्मनोवायुसमैर्जवे ॥","meaning":{"en":"He also gave a chariot yoked with divine horses, bearing the banner of the foremost of monkeys, drawn by silver-white gandharva horses with golden garlands, bright as white clouds and swift as mind and wind."}},{"n":9,"text":"सर्वोपकरणैर्युक्तमजय्यं देवदानवैः ।\nभानुमन्तं महाघोषं सर्वभूतमनोहरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"It was fitted with every equipment, unconquerable by gods and danavas, radiant, of great rumble, and delightful to all beings,"}},{"n":10,"text":"ससर्ज यत्स्वतपसा भौवनो भुवनप्रभुः ।\nप्रजापतिरनिर्देश्यं यस्य रूपं रवेरिव ॥","meaning":{"en":"which Bhauvana, the lord of the world and Prajapati, made by his own austerity, and whose form, like the sun's, could not be described,"}},{"n":11,"text":"यं स्म सोमः समारुह्य दानवानजयत्प्रभुः ।\nनगमेघप्रतीकाशं ज्वलन्तमिव च श्रिया ॥","meaning":{"en":"and which King Soma mounted when he conquered the danavas, like a cloud-covered mountain and blazing with splendor."}},{"n":12,"text":"आश्रिता तं रथश्रेष्ठं शक्रायुधसमा शुभा ।\nतापनीया सुरुचिरा ध्वजयष्टिरनुत्तमा ॥","meaning":{"en":"On that best of chariots stood a banner-pole, excellent and golden, bright like Indra's weapon, matchless."}},{"n":13,"text":"तस्यां तु वानरो दिव्यः सिंहशार्दूललक्षणः ।\nविनर्दन्निव तत्रस्थः संस्थितो मूर्ध्न्यशोभत ॥","meaning":{"en":"On it was a divine monkey, marked like a lion or tiger, who seemed to roar from his place, shining at the top."}},{"n":14,"text":"ध्वजे भूतानि तत्रासन्विविधानि महान्ति च ।\nनादेन रिपुसैन्यानां येषां संज्ञा प्रणश्यति ॥","meaning":{"en":"On that banner were beings of many kinds and great size, whose roar made enemy armies lose their senses."}},{"n":15,"text":"स तं नानापताकाभिः शोभितं रथमुत्तमम् ।\nप्रदक्षिणमुपावृत्य दैवतेभ्यः प्रणम्य च ॥","meaning":{"en":"Circling that chariot, adorned with many flags, keeping it to his right, and bowing to the gods,"}},{"n":16,"text":"संनद्धः कवची खड्गी बद्धगोधाङ्गुलित्रवान् ।\nआरुरोह रथं पार्थो विमानं सुकृती यथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Partha, armored, with sword, with finger-guard and arm-guard bound on, mounted the chariot like a man of merit boarding a heavenly car."}},{"n":17,"text":"तच्च दिव्यं धनुःश्रेष्ठं ब्रह्मणा निर्मितं पुरा ।\nगाण्डीवमुपसंगृह्य बभूव मुदितोऽर्जुनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Taking up that excellent divine bow Gandiva, which Brahma had made long ago, Arjuna was glad."}},{"n":18,"text":"हुताशनं नमस्कृत्य ततस्तदपि वीर्यवान् ।\nजग्राह बलमास्थाय ज्यया च युयुजे धनुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having bowed to Agni, the mighty one then took it with strength and strung the bow."}},{"n":19,"text":"मौर्व्यां तु युज्यमानायां बलिना पाण्डवेन ह ।\nयेऽशृण्वन्कूजितं तत्र तेषां वै व्यथितं मनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As the strong Pandava strung it, those who heard the twang of the bowstring were shaken in mind."}},{"n":20,"text":"लब्ध्वा रथं धनुश्चैव तथाक्षय्यौ महेषुधी ।\nबभूव कल्यः कौन्तेयः प्रहृष्टः साह्यकर्मणि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having obtained the chariot, the bow and the two great inexhaustible quivers, the son of Kunti became ready and glad for the work of helping."}},{"n":21,"text":"वज्रनाभं ततश्चक्रं ददौ कृष्णाय पावकः ।\nआग्नेयमस्त्रं दयितं स च कल्योऽभवत्तदा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Agni gave Krishna a discus with a thunderbolt-like hub, a beloved fiery weapon, and Krishna too became ready."}},{"n":22,"text":"अब्रवीत्पावकश्चैनमेतेन मधुसूदन ।\nअमानुषानपि रणे विजेष्यसि न संशयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Agni said to him: With this, Madhusudana, you will overcome even beings not human in battle, there is no doubt."}},{"n":23,"text":"अनेन त्वं मनुष्याणां देवानामपि चाहवे ।\nरक्षःपिशाचदैत्यानां नागानां चाधिकः सदा ।\nभविष्यसि न संदेहः प्रवरारिनिबर्हणे ॥","meaning":{"en":"With this you will always surpass men and gods in combat, and rakshasas, pishachas, daityas and nagas, and there is no doubt that you will destroy the best of foes."}},{"n":24,"text":"क्षिप्तं क्षिप्तं रणे चैतत्त्वया माधव शत्रुषु ।\nहत्वाप्रतिहतं संख्ये पाणिमेष्यति ते पुनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Each time you hurl it at enemies in battle, Madhava, it will kill them and return to your hand unhindered."}},{"n":25,"text":"वरुणश्च ददौ तस्मै गदामशनिनिःस्वनाम् ।\nदैत्यान्तकरणीं घोरां नाम्ना कौमोदकीं हरेः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Varuna also gave Hari the fearsome mace named Kaumodaki, which roars like thunder and destroys the Daityas."}},{"n":26,"text":"ततः पावकमब्रूतां प्रहृष्टौ कृष्णपाण्डवौ ।\nकृतास्त्रौ शस्त्रसंपन्नौ रथिनौ ध्वजिनावपि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Krishna and the Pandava, delighted, said to Agni, now armed with weapons, in chariot and with banner:"}},{"n":27,"text":"कल्यौ स्वो भगवन्योद्धुमपि सर्वैः सुरासुरैः ।\nकिं पुनर्वज्रिणैकेन पन्नगार्थे युयुत्सुना ॥","meaning":{"en":"Holy one, we are able to fight even all the gods and asuras together, let alone the wielder of the thunderbolt alone, who fights for the sake of the serpent."}},{"text":"अर्जुन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Arjuna said:"}},{"n":28,"text":"चक्रमस्त्रं च वार्ष्णेयो विसृजन्युधि वीर्यवान् ।\nत्रिषु लोकेषु तन्नास्ति यन्न जीयाज्जनार्दनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"When valiant Vrishni hurls his discus and weapon in battle, there is nothing in the three worlds that Janardana would not conquer."}},{"n":29,"text":"गाण्डीवं धनुरादाय तथाक्षय्यौ महेषुधी ।\nअहमप्युत्सहे लोकान्विजेतुं युधि पावक ॥","meaning":{"en":"Taking the bow Gandiva and the two great inexhaustible quivers, I too am eager to conquer the worlds in battle, Agni."}},{"n":30,"text":"सर्वतः परिवार्यैनं दावेन महता प्रभो ।\nकामं संप्रज्वलाद्यैव कल्यौ स्वः साह्यकर्मणि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Surround this forest on every side, O lord, with a great blaze; burn as you wish this very day, for we are ready to help."}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":31,"text":"एवमुक्तः स भगवान्दाशार्हेणार्जुनेन च ।\nतैजसं रूपमास्थाय दावं दग्धुं प्रचक्रमे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Thus addressed by the Dasharha and Arjuna, the holy one took on his fiery form and began to burn the forest."}},{"n":32,"text":"सर्वतः परिवार्याथ सप्तार्चिर्ज्वलनस्तदा ।\nददाह खाण्डवं क्रुद्धो युगान्तमिव दर्शयन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Surrounding it on every side, the seven-flamed Agni, enraged, burned Khandava, as if showing the end of the age."}},{"n":33,"text":"परिगृह्य समाविष्टस्तद्वनं भरतर्षभ ।\nमेघस्तनितनिर्घोषं सर्वभूतानि निर्दहन् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Entering and enveloping that forest, O bull of the Bharatas, he burned all beings, with a roar like thundering clouds."}},{"n":34,"text":"दह्यतस्तस्य विबभौ रूपं दावस्य भारत ।\nमेरोरिव नगेन्द्रस्य काञ्चनस्य महाद्युतेः ॥","meaning":{"en":"As the forest burned, its aspect shone, Bharata, like that of Mount Meru, king of mountains, golden and of great splendor."}}]}]}